CVE-2023-28147 triggers when a client sends a GraphQL introspection fragment (`__type`) with aliased selections:
```
query { __type(name:"User") { fields { name alias: name } } }
```
The server’s response collapses aliased fields into a single `fields` array. An attacker iteratively queries:
```
fragment A on User { friends { ...A } }
fragment B on User { friends { ...B } }
```
The resolver merges `A` and `B` fields into the same selection set, effectively bypassing field maxDepth (default 10). Exploitation via `graphql-ide`:
1. Open GraphiQL at `/graphiql`.
2. Paste query:
```
{__type(name:"Query"){
  fields{name,args{name}}
  }
}
```
3. Append aliased fragments until >500 field traversals.
Mitigation: disable introspection (`graphql-playground: {introspection: false}`), set `maxDepth: 10` and `maxAliases: 5`, patch Apollo 2.17.5, and enable query cost analysis (`queryCost: true`).

